WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.220
Binance suffered a suspected $6.3 billion hack today, putting crypto holdings of users worldwide at risk. This is Omni View, Episode 221. A Russian newspaper forced to close a siege in Yemen and American voters' ranking corruption, then understanding the issue. Analytics firms named a North Korean hacking unit, Trader Trader, as responsible for the Binance theft. Binance is a major cryptocurrency exchange, a platform where people buy and sell digital assets.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.200
threats. The theft is being treated as potentially the largest cryptocurrency exchange hack on

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:40.560
record. BBC Asia frames the event as a significant blow to the crypto sector and links it directly

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.820
to state-linked actors, meaning groups tied to a government. That reading stresses how

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:50.600
hard it is to secure digital assets against sophisticated groups that operate across borders.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.900
Similar thefts have followed a pattern in which the proceeds help pay for equipment and

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:00.900
for the day-to-day running of the groups involved. Recovery work is only beginning to be described

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.780
in public. Tracing of the stolen funds and whatever responds to the exchange issues,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:11.536
will be watched in the coming days. Novaya Gazeta, the independent Russian newspaper,

00:01:11.876 --> 00:01:16.716
stated it will cease operations. It cited searches of its editor's home and the detention

00:01:16.716 --> 00:01:22.596
of a journalist. Editor-in-chief Sergei Sokolov said Russian Special Services forced the shutdown.

00:01:22.596 --> 00:01:29.316
The Guardian and France 24 described the closure as the end of one of Russia's last major independent outlets,

00:01:29.896 --> 00:01:34.656
and they note the paper's history of critical reporting and its former editor's Nobel recognition.

00:01:34.996 --> 00:01:39.176
They also point to a broader tightening of media control since 2022.

00:01:39.896 --> 00:01:48.536
The paper had already faced license revocation and foreign agent status after cutting production inside Russia, following the 2022 offensive on Ukraine.

00:01:48.536 --> 00:01:53.156
train. The foreign agent label and the loss of its media license came in the same year.

00:01:53.836 --> 00:01:57.956
Sokolov said in a YouTube video that the authorities had forced the editorial team to

00:01:57.956 --> 00:02:04.156
end its work after a colleague, Oleg Roldogen was detained in April. The charge was unlawful

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:09.496
access to computerized information. Remaining staff will try to move to exile operations

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:13.696
if possible. The paper's servers will be shut down on November 9th.

00:02:13.696 --> 00:02:18.917
Taiz Yemen's third largest city has been under a month-long siege, according to its

00:02:18.917 --> 00:02:19.317
governor.

00:02:19.997 --> 00:02:24.477
Nebel Shamsan said Houthi forces have cut oxygen, food, and water supplies.

00:02:25.017 --> 00:02:30.037
He said rubbish is piling up, landfill sites have become inaccessible, and massacres are

00:02:30.037 --> 00:02:31.197
taking place in the city.

00:02:31.677 --> 00:02:34.377
He appealed for international action to lift the blockade.

00:02:34.837 --> 00:02:38.737
His briefing presents those shortages as deliberate deprivation of civilians.

00:02:38.737 --> 00:02:43.437
citizens. International organizations will be pressed to increase humanitarian access to

00:02:43.437 --> 00:02:48.969
the city. American voters from both parties now list corruption alongside the economy and

00:02:48.969 --> 00:02:54.809
gas prices as a leading issue. The Christian Science Monitor reports. Candidates in competitive

00:02:54.809 --> 00:02:59.549
races have begun running advertisements focused on the topic, and they are discussing it on

00:02:59.549 --> 00:03:04.509
the campaign trail as well. The Monitor frames the rise and concern as a rare cross-party

00:03:04.509 --> 00:03:08.889
development that could influence turnout and messaging in the final days before the election.

00:03:09.669 --> 00:03:14.649
Everything turns on whether voters treat corruption as a problem of weak rules or as a problem

00:03:14.649 --> 00:03:20.469
of government that has grown too large. Candidates and analysts who emphasize institutional safeguards

00:03:20.469 --> 00:03:25.409
argue that stronger disclosure rules and independent oversight bodies would reduce opportunities

00:03:25.409 --> 00:03:31.069
for misuse of public funds and restore trust in elected office. Those advocates acknowledge

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:33.709
that enforcement remains uneven across states.

00:03:34.189 --> 00:03:37.249
Candidates focused on reducing regulatory reach argue

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:40.049
that fewer government programs and lower spending levels

00:03:40.049 --> 00:03:41.709
would shrink the scope for corruption

00:03:42.019 --> 00:03:45.269
by limiting the resources available for political allocation.

00:03:45.689 --> 00:03:47.629
They note that this approach may leave

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:50.149
some public services underfunded in the short term.

00:03:50.809 --> 00:03:52.429
Polling in the final week will show

00:03:52.429 --> 00:03:54.989
whether corruption messaging shifts voter priorities

00:03:54.989 --> 00:03:55.909
in key districts.

00:03:56.942 --> 00:03:59.462
Nationwide reported UK house prices rose

00:03:59.462 --> 00:04:06.722
just 0.5% in the year to October. The weakest pace since 2024. The Guardian links that slowdown

00:04:06.722 --> 00:04:14.562
to increase borrowing costs after recent rate movements. The average price stood at 273,566 pounds,

00:04:15.102 --> 00:04:20.702
unchanged from the previous month. Annual growth had been 0.8% in the year to September.

00:04:21.382 --> 00:04:26.542
Higher mortgage rates are cited as the main factor deterring buyers, with potential purchasers stepping

00:04:26.542 --> 00:04:32.362
back amid elevated financing expenses. Monthly data releases will show whether the trend continues

00:04:32.362 --> 00:04:39.695
into winter. Pre-market trading sent Amazon shares down 7% and Intel shares down 25% after both

00:04:39.695 --> 00:04:44.895
companies reported earnings. For Intel, a drop of about a quarter of the share price before the

00:04:44.895 --> 00:04:50.695
opening bell. CNBC reports the sell-off reflects broader nervousness about whether heavy capital

00:04:50.695 --> 00:04:56.695
expenditure by technology firms will generate profits quickly enough. Investors express concern over

00:04:56.695 --> 00:05:02.395
the scale of spending on artificial intelligence, or AI infrastructure and its near-term returns.

00:05:02.955 --> 00:05:07.515
The moves came amid questions about the pace at which AI-related investments translate

00:05:07.515 --> 00:05:13.495
into revenue growth. Hong Kong's transport department confirmed that Uber, Didi Chucksing,

00:05:14.095 --> 00:05:18.995
Singapore-based Tata, and others applied for ride-hailing licenses, progress worth knowing

00:05:18.995 --> 00:05:23.775
under a new safety and insurance regime. Eight companies submitted applications before

00:05:23.775 --> 00:05:29.275
the deadline, and AMAP operated by Ali Baba Group holding also confirmed its application.

00:05:29.915 --> 00:05:34.835
South China Morning Post coverage notes this as the first formal step toward licensed operations

00:05:34.835 --> 00:05:40.535
in a market previously dominated by unlicensed services. The firms drew on global operational

00:05:40.535 --> 00:05:45.915
experience while meeting local requirements under the updated framework. Approval timelines and

00:05:45.915 --> 00:05:51.582
final service conditions remain subject to government review. Elsewhere, Nigeria's National

00:05:51.582 --> 00:05:58.102
Council on Climate Change will pursue global funding to create 840,000 jobs by 2060 while

00:05:58.102 --> 00:06:00.422
attending the UN conference COP31.

00:06:01.182 --> 00:06:06.822
All Africa reports, Uganda's President Musevani invited Egyptian investors into infrastructure

00:06:06.822 --> 00:06:11.042
and manufacturing, highlighting value addition and industrial capacity.

00:06:11.582 --> 00:06:17.042
A Sudan investigation by the Center for Information Resilience identified 25 commanders linked

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:22.802
to reported sexual violence sites, mapping RSF and Sudanese armed forces officers at five

00:06:22.802 --> 00:06:28.802
locations during documented abuse periods, Al Jazeera reports. Kenya is preparing to host

00:06:28.802 --> 00:06:34.822
the 2029 World Athletics Championships in Nairobi as the first African venue, ending decades

00:06:34.822 --> 00:06:38.862
without the event on the continent and aiming to build on the country's distance-running

00:06:38.862 --> 00:06:39.302
record.

00:06:40.042 --> 00:06:45.662
Venezuela's Machado, the Nobel Laureate, urged 2027 elections after returning from exile,

00:06:45.662 --> 00:06:49.262
while criticizing a recent U.S. oil agreement with Caracas.

00:06:50.237 --> 00:06:55.217
To really understand how cryptocurrency exchanges manage large-scale thefts, start with

00:06:55.217 --> 00:06:58.337
the chain of custody decisions made long before any breach.

00:06:58.877 --> 00:07:03.297
The common misunderstanding is that a major hack is simply a sudden technical failure.

00:07:03.997 --> 00:07:09.397
Exchanges typically hold the majority of customer assets in offline cold wallets that require

00:07:09.397 --> 00:07:11.597
multiple human approvals to move funds.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:17.297
They keep only a small fraction in online hot wallets, which stay connected so daily trading

00:07:17.297 --> 00:07:17.837
can settle.

00:07:18.517 --> 00:07:22.977
When coins are stolen, they often move through mixers or cross-chain bridges that obscure

00:07:22.977 --> 00:07:23.537
ownership.

00:07:24.357 --> 00:07:28.597
Investigators then follow wallet addresses on the public ledger rather than real-world

00:07:28.597 --> 00:07:28.937
names.

00:07:29.557 --> 00:07:34.357
That work is done by blockchain analysis firms, which cluster addresses that appear to

00:07:34.357 --> 00:07:35.377
be controlled together.

00:07:36.057 --> 00:07:40.317
Theft of this kind has also been used as a revenue stream that bypasses traditional

00:07:40.317 --> 00:07:45.757
financial sanctions. Because the ledger is public, the coins can still be mapped after the fact

00:07:45.757 --> 00:07:50.897
even when they cannot be seized at once. That is why I claim that an exchange loss funds

00:07:50.897 --> 00:07:56.197
is not the same as the coins vanishing. They can remain visible even when recovery is slow.

00:07:56.837 --> 00:08:01.797
If a report names a particular unit, look at whether the attribution rests on those wallet

00:08:01.797 --> 00:08:07.017
clustering patterns or on a broader intelligence assessment. Next time a theft is reported,

00:08:07.017 --> 00:08:11.597
Look for whether the exchange has published an on-chain address for any recovered portion

00:08:11.597 --> 00:08:12.637
of the stolen assets.

00:08:13.496 --> 00:08:18.776
Before settling on the scale, or who was responsible, read a second outlet from another region

00:08:19.116 --> 00:08:23.216
and prefer an exchange statement or a regulatory filing over the first headline.

00:08:23.916 --> 00:08:28.956
Amazon and Intel's full market reaction and any revised guidance from the companies will

00:08:28.956 --> 00:08:30.556
be watched on the next trading day.

